internal backup 3.7V DC; 5200mAh; Battery\n- MS2500/MV110 LV: 24–36V AC/DC, 45–66 Hz, internal backup 3.7V DC; 5200mAh; Battery\n- MS2500/MV110 LLV: 10–48 V DC, no frequency (-), no backup (-)\n\nThis is a configuration axis (power supply variant: HV/LV/LLV). I could model this as config_level entries with axis \"power_supply_variant\".\n\nAlso software version V.1.04.0005.0004, CRC 9BA34F3B, cut-off 0.2%, detection empty pipe on.\n\nOther characteristics:\n- Measuring principle: Electromagnetic water meter\n- Temperature class: varies by liner:\n  - PTFE: T90; T50; T30\n  - Rilsan: T50; T30 from DN50\n  - Ebonite: T50; T30 from DN200\n  - polypropylene: T50; T30\n- Water pressure class: MAP16\n- Pressure loss class: Δp40\n- Reverse flow: designed to measure\n- Environmental class: O (-25 to +55 °C)\n- Electromagnetic environment: E1, E2\n- Mechanical class: B, O\n- Maximum admissible temperature: PTFE 90°C; Polypropylen/Rilsan/Ebonite 50°C\n- Maximum admissible pressure: 1.6 MPa\n- Orientation limitation: any\n- Indicating range: 9 999 999 m³\n- Resolution of indicating device: 0.01 m³\n- Resolution of device for rapid testing: \"-\" (missing — omit per rule 8)\n- EUT testing requirements: Category: Electromagnetic water meter, Case: Case D\n- Installation: connection type flanged, min straight inlet 0 mm, outlet 0 mm, flow profile sensitivity class U0D0, flow conditioner No, orientation any, length 550 mm\n\nMPE:\n- MPE_l: ±3% (class 1), ±5% (class 2)\n- MPE_u: ±1 (class 1) ±2 (class 2) % for water ≤ 30°C; ±2 (class1) ±3 (class 2) % for > 30°C\n\nThese are class-dependent — could go in config_level with axis \"accuracy_class\". That seems reasonable.\n\nEnvironmental class: O with range -25 to +55 °C. I'll record as environmental_class: \"O\" and maybe operating temperature range.\n\nLet me structure the JSON:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-CZ1-2022.02\"\n  },\n  \"manufacturers\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Hemina SPA\",\n     