of 16 pages\"). Include.\n\nLet me also decide model_family. family_name: \"MS2500 / MV110\" or null. Models: two entries differing by Q3/Q1. Include model attributes? I could put attributes on models: {\"q3_over_q1\": 250} etc. But characteristics.model_level already covers that. I'll keep models minimal with maybe attributes.\n\nAlso, the model number includes DN350 — the fragment says \"Nominal diameter: 350\". Since temperature class mentions other DN sizes for liner availability, but this table is DN350. Keep type_level nominal_diameter = 350.\n\nNow let me also handle \"Internal backup source\": \"3,7V DC; 5200mAh; Battery\" → decimal comma → 3.7. Split into:\n- config_level: attribute internal_backup_battery_voltage, axis power_supply_variant, values: [{condition \"MS2500 / MV110 HV\", value 3.7, unit_symbol \"V\"}, {condition \"MS2500 / MV110 LV\", value 3.7, unit_symbol \"V\"}]\n- config_level: attribute internal_backup_battery_capacity, values 5200 mAh for HV and LV.\n- internal_backup_type: \"Battery\" for HV, LV.\n\nMaybe simpler to keep as one string value \"3.7 V DC; 5200 mAh battery\". But rule 3 says pull units out. Splitting is more compliant. I'll split into voltage and capacity.\n\nCut-off: 0,2% → 0.2 %.\n\nMPE entries as config_level:\n\n{\n  \"attribute\": \"maximum_permitted_error_lower_zone\",\n  \"axis\": \"accuracy_class\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"accuracy class 1\", \"value\": {\"min\": -3, \"max\": 3}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"accuracy class 2\", \"value\": {\"min\": -5, \"max\": 5}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"}\n  ]\n}\n\n{\n  \"attribute\": \"maximum_permitted_error_upper_zone\",\n  \"axis\": \"accuracy_class and water_temperature\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"class 1, water temperature ≤ 30 °C\", \"value\": {\"min\": -1, \"max\": 1}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"class 2, water temperature ≤ 30 °C\", \"value\": {\"min\": -2, \"max\": 2}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"},\n    {\"co